{%- comment -%}
  PDP — Zip code delivery date estimator.

  Renders the zip input plus a Standard and Express estimated delivery date.

  NOTE ON DATA SOURCE
  A theme cannot read Shopify shipping settings at runtime. The only storefront
  endpoint for live rates is /cart/shipping_rates.json, which requires a
  non-empty cart — a PDP visitor usually has none. So the transit windows below
  are theme settings, seeded from the store's real delivery profile
  (USA DOMESTIC: Standard, Standard free, Express). Keep them in sync with
  Settings → Shipping and delivery, or move to an app if live rates are needed.

  Accepts:
    standard_min / standard_max  — business days, drive the dates (never printed)
    express_min  / express_max   — business days, drive the dates (never printed)
    standard_label / express_label — service names, e.g. Foreign Air
    standard_price / express_price — free text, so "Free over $150" is sayable
    cutoff_hour                  — 0-23, read in delivery_timezone
    delivery_timezone            — IANA zone the warehouse keeps, e.g. America/Los_Angeles
    free_threshold               — money amount for complimentary standard
{%- endcomment -%}

<div
  class="dest"
  data-delivery-estimator
  data-standard-min="{{ standard_min | default: 3 }}"
  data-standard-max="{{ standard_max | default: 5 }}"
  data-express-min="{{ express_min | default: 1 }}"
  data-express-max="{{ express_max | default: 2 }}"
  data-cutoff-hour="{{ cutoff_hour | default: 13 }}"
  data-timezone="{{ delivery_timezone | default: 'America/Los_Angeles' }}"
  data-country="{{ localization.country.iso_code | default: 'US' }}"
>
  <p class="dest__label">
    <span class="dest__pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    Delivery date guarantee
  </p>

  <div class="dest__entry">
    <label class="dest__hint" for="dest-zip">Enter your zip code here</label>
    <div class="dest__row">
      <input
        type="text"
        id="dest-zip"
        class="dest__input"
        inputmode="numeric"
        autocomplete="postal-code"
        maxlength="10"
        placeholder="00000"
        data-dest-zip
      >
      <button type="button" class="dest__apply" data-dest-apply>Apply</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Two rows, spec-table shape: service name and price on the left, the resolved
    dates on the right. The business-day counts are deliberately absent — the
    dates already say when it lands, and "3–5 business days" next to
    "Aug 6 – Aug 10" is the same fact twice in a weaker unit. The day counts
    still drive the arithmetic, they just aren't restated as copy.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="dest__results" data-dest-results hidden>
    <div class="dest__tier">
      <span class="dest__tier-label">{{ standard_label | default: 'Foreign Air' }}</span>
      <span class="dest__tier-price">{{ standard_price | default: '$10' }}</span>
      <span class="dest__tier-date" data-dest-standard></span>
    </div>
    <div class="dest__tier">
      <span class="dest__tier-label">{{ express_label | default: 'Express Air' }}</span>
      <span class="dest__tier-price">{{ express_price | default: '$20' }}</span>
      <span class="dest__tier-date" data-dest-express></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="dest__error" data-dest-error hidden>Enter a valid zip code to see delivery dates.</p>
</div>
